{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463304-need-clarifications-regarding-moon-bridge-moon-path","id":1463304,"title":"Need Clarifications regarding Moon Bridge/Moon Path","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-10T04:31:35-07:00","id":1463304,"title":"Need Clarifications regarding Moon Bridge/Moon Path","content":"Hi team,<br /> <br /> I wanted something clarified regarding moon bridges or moon paths. I'm aware they open up a path for Garou to travel through in split seconds by the power of the moon.<br /> Some clarity on the following Gift would be appreicated;<br /> <br /> w20 page 170<br /> \u2022 Bridge Walker (Level Four) \u2014 The Galliard may create minor moon bridges through which she alone can travel. Such travel takes one percent of the time the journey would take normally, allowing the werewolf to disappear from in front of a foe and reappear behind it instantly. These moon bridges are not protected by Lunes, and may attract the interest of spirits. A Lune teaches this Gift. System: The player spends one Gnosis point to create the bridge. The moon bridge lasts for only one passage, unless the player spends an additional three Willpower, in which case it lasts until the next full moon. The maximum distance that can be traversed by the bridge is the Garou\u2019s Gnosis in miles (1.6 km per Gnosis dot).<br /> <br /> 1: Can these be opened in the material world (skinlands, earth)<br /> 2: Can these be opened when there exists no moonlight? (utter darkness and/or broad sunlight)<br /> 3: Can there be additional expenditures to allow other characters to be taken through?<br /> 4: Opening the moon bridge till next full moon, does it allow just about anyone to pass through?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12544-diplo","name":"diplo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12544_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T06:00:38-07:00","id":1463306,"title":"","content":"Answers, in my opinion:<br /> 1. Yes. The Gift can do this. And Moon Bridges from Caern to Caern can also have their Portals in the material world, although the caern spirit and the garou who holds the Gatekeeper office might have the ability to prohibit this. The comic in the beginning of the 2nd Edition Core Rules indicates portals from the physical world....<br /> 2. Yes. The Gift/Rite/Charm open a direct portal to the Atherical Realm of the near umbra, where the bridge is rising, reaching the top and is descending to the other portal in a beam of moon light and the Moon is usually visible right above the moon bridge, with the optical illusion one could just reach the moon with one's arm. The situation in the physical world or penumbra or umbra realm where the portal opens is irrelevant - when it comes to light. It might be relevant whether or not there are protection Rite or other effects in place. Spirit and Correspondence might both allow to shield against a moon bridge for example. Prime, too, I guess.<br /> 3. Once the Bridge is established, basically a whole bunch of people can use it, if you are talking about the gift. If the Galliard didn't spend the three additional willpower to make the Gift effect last, he better be the last one to exit the moon bridge, or anyone behind him might find themselves on a collapsing bridge - which means they are falling down, in the aetherial realm. But moon bridges are possibly broad enough, for one person to bypass another. Especially in homid or lupus form.<br /> 4. It there aren't other provisions to protect the portal, yes. Portals, that is, for the bridge in in essence bidirectional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T11:12:39-07:00","id":1463329,"title":"","content":"Since that Gift says &quot;which she alone can travel&quot;, it seems pretty clear that only the specific Galliard who creates that minor moon bridge can use it. Though obviously spirits in the umbral void the moon bridge passes through can visit if the ST sees fit. Therefore, I would vote &quot;no&quot; to questions 3 and 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T12:18:21-07:00","id":1463337,"title":"","content":"I agree on 1 &amp; 2.<br /> <br /> On 3 &amp; 4, the Gift explicitly says, as quoted above, that only the Galliard with the Gift can travel on the bridge created by it.<br /> <br /> So #3 is out as there's no general way to spend more on a Gift to have it to more than it says it does.<br /> <br /> #4 is weirder because there's a conflict between the stated function of the Gift, and how moonbridges work metaphysically. A simple way to resolve this is that the Gift acts like a Gatekeeper, and bars anyone but the Galliard from entering the portals of the bridge. However, the bridge would still be subject to intrusion via the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T13:13:40-07:00","id":1463345,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but sure, the Gift is only for the Galliard. I missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}